{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question","id":56544,"title":"Skin Dancer Question...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-23T20:03:14-08:00","id":56544,"title":"Skin Dancer Question...","content":"Right so Skin Dancers are made from taking the skins of 5 garou and a ritual ja? So in knowing that, if a Skin Dancer takes all the skins from bsds, do they incur the mutation as well? Or do they just take the fur coloration and the ability to shape shift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:12:23-08:00","id":56547,"title":"","content":"You look like what you skin in your other forms, so... don't skin ugly, mutated BSDs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-23T20:29:29-08:00","id":56555,"title":"","content":"I guess if you took the choice bits from certain spirals it wouldnt be so bad. OR if you were bad ass enough to kill a Cluithi.. that would take some serious skill though. Or an incredibly lucky kinfolk with a high powered rifle from a distance far enough away that the rest of that pack (cause you KNOW they move in packs) wont come get you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T05:46:17-08:00","id":56676,"title":"","content":"I always used the latter interruption; When the dancer takes in the pelts, the fur in each area differs based on the donors original pelt but its not a direct representation. However, when using BSD pelts, I have them start more tainted as they have absorbed more then what the ritual already gives them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:42:52-08:00","id":56751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=56676#post56676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always used the latter interruption; When the dancer takes in the pelts, the fur in each area differs based on the donors original pelt but its not a direct representation. However, when using BSD pelts, I have them start more tainted as they have absorbed more then what the ritual already gives them.</div> </div> </div> </div>More tainted than you would be for hunting down and killing Garou to skin and use the pelts of in a horribly tainted rite? You're only not tainted if they all give their skins and lives willingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T07:54:40-08:00","id":56758,"title":"","content":"So is THAT why Gaia invented Harano? ;0)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-24T08:18:41-08:00","id":56775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=56751#post56751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More tainted than you would be for hunting down and killing Garou to skin and use the pelts of in a horribly tainted rite? You're only not tainted if they all give their skins and lives willingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Skin Dancers start tainted, but taint can be acquired and lost, therefore there are levels of Taint. You have temporary and permanent ratings of taint for all 3 trait, most Storytellers just don't want the extra overhead so they just say you are or you aren't tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-26T23:50:31-08:00","id":58556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=56775#post56775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, Skin Dancers start tainted, but taint can be acquired and lost, therefore there are levels of Taint. You have temporary and permanent ratings of taint for all 3 trait, most Storytellers just don't want the extra overhead so they just say you are or you aren't tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite.<br /> <br /> There is a distinction between rules/mechanic and InGame-choice of words.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, there are taint backgrounds, first presented in the Player's Guide to Garou (and as far as I know, only there). As backgrounds these character traits are probably supposed to be semi-permanent stats. Wouldn't spend points on them, if a Rite of Cleansing (or one of those other cleansing rites) would get rid of it. So, while they are named &quot;Tainted&quot;, they are more like 'corruption', in a sense that they are lasting, as opposed to the statement, that places, victims and possibly observers of wyrm-deeds can acquire wyrm-taint (for example stated in the &quot;Sense Wyrm isn't sense evil&quot;-sidebar).<br /> There is a mechanic named &quot;Corruption&quot; in WoD:Outcasts. It is pretty much like VtM's Humanity for Ronin, so they have a mechanic that shows their struggle not to fall to the wyrm. While the stat &quot;Corruption&quot; is meant to change, like humanity, it is also a semi-permanent characteristic, that is not simply changed via ingame magics, but through role-playing and possibly expenditure of experience points.<br /> Finally, there is a Flaw named &quot;Wyrm-Tainted&quot;. It also represents a lasting kind of taint, regardless of the name. And it is supposed to be a bad thing to have that kind of taint, hence the Flaw, so I never found the background suitable for the game...<br /> <br /> <br /> As far as skindancer go, they also have a kind of permanent taint. The Rite is rotten to the core and it changes the very being of a person. Being subject to the Rite isn't like acquiring a wyrm taint for working at the suicide ward of a psychiatry wing. It doesn't come off with a Rite of Cleansing. It is also written, that this is kind of the dilemma of the Skin Dancers. Some were, like Haight, hating the garou but now, that they are garou themselves, understand their burden, their motivations and more than just a few are willing, with all their heart and soul to defend gaia, as garou should. But the mark of evil is burned into their essence permanently.<br /> <br /> <br /> There isn't a mechanic that keeps track of Taints of the Triat like there is a system for keeping track of renown, though. And there isn't a mention of permanent or temporary taint either. There is just taint, and a ST has to figure out for himself how lasting it should be, depending on the circumstances and the mood of the game he is running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T01:41:40-08:00","id":58584,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that a Skin Dancer <i>might</i> be able to remove his or her taint, but only by going through a Chronicle-spanning quest to do so, and garnering the support of all of the Tribes affected by the Rite, as well as several high-powered Wyld spirits. This is the stuff of powerful Storytelling, not some simple mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T10:52:00-08:00","id":58886,"title":"","content":"Minotour could demand his children go through erebus to remove the taint. That's something I was going to have Lion demand of a reborn White Howler tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T12:54:40-08:00","id":59029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=58886#post58886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minotour could demand his children go through erebus to remove the taint. That's something I was going to have Lion demand of a reborn White Howler tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erebus is powerless to do anything unless, in your heart of hearts, you know that you have transgressed and genuinely wish to make amends with those you have wronged. Not because you want redemption, but because you desire a change back to purity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T15:02:48-08:00","id":59177,"title":"","content":"I apologize, Heinrich is correct. The system we were using is variation of the Autonomy system used in Possessed and the Corruption system Heinrich mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T20:21:33-08:00","id":59423,"title":"","content":"so you're telling me that a character can't just dump themselves into a planet of molten silver and just come out of it all &quot;LOOK GUYZ I AINT O' DA WYRM NO MOE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T05:16:28-08:00","id":60646,"title":"","content":"The one thing I don't get is when BSD go into Erebus they come out Ronin with no access to the gifts and rites they had before, but what would happen to a Skin Dancer then? I think some of the tribe could benefit from Erebus as the 4 way schism leaves 3 parts either working in Gaias favor or staying neutral so they could legitimately be remorseful. I can see why no SD would want to try, the thought that it could burn away the magic that is making them what they are, they would lose what they worked so hard and be back where they started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T05:39:02-08:00","id":60658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=60646#post60646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I don't get is when BSD go into Erebus they come out Ronin with no access to the gifts and rites they had before, but what would happen to a Skin Dancer then? I think some of the tribe could benefit from Erebus as the 4 way schism leaves 3 parts either working in Gaias favor or staying neutral so they could legitimately be remorseful. I can see why no SD would want to try, the thought that it could burn away the magic that is making them what they are, they would lose what they worked so hard and be back where they started.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the biggest question to ask -before- we even start talking about Erebus, is whether or not the Skin Dancer has to hunt the pelts themselves. From the revised books, this was said to be one of the component for the rite. However, Skinner SAS, which is to date the most in-depth look at Skin Dancers outside Haight, implies otherwise. The pack in it is said to basically stockpile pelts for any new convert.<br /> <br /> If we go by the former, then the whole process is indeed quite clearly so corrupt that the SD would not seek redemption. After all, they killed 5 werewolves to become one. But if we go by the W20 view, then the situation becomes far more complicated. If the convert does not have to hunt their own pelts, just to get the ritual performed (the SAS implied even THAT does not require the kin themselves to do know it) they essentially have only chosen to reject their role as kinfolk. A SD from this kind of source could easily as a garou see why their family became so cruel, and try to redeem themselves.<br /> <br /> There is also the level of taint involved. SDs are not BSD level tainted, so I would assume they could be purified outside Erebus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T05:50:05-08:00","id":60663,"title":"","content":"Ana Mizuki, how about another point to think about, WHO the donor of the pelts are? Killing BSD for any reason does not result in becoming Tainted by all accords and I was just reading Hammer and Klaive last night and there are tribal fetishes which use bones of fallen enemies. So if a Skin Dancer uses BSD pelts to for her ritual, is she tainted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T06:41:17-08:00","id":60706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=60663#post60663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ana Mizuki, how about another point to think about, WHO the donor of the pelts are? Killing BSD for any reason does not result in becoming Tainted by all accords and I was just reading Hammer and Klaive last night and there are tribal fetishes which use bones of fallen enemies. So if a Skin Dancer uses BSD pelts to for her ritual, is she tainted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because it's a tainted ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T08:06:09-08:00","id":60781,"title":"","content":"One thing I am unclear on, do the pelts used need to be harvested for the ritual or could a tribe in trouble from dwindling numbers, not sure why I think Uktena first, harvest the pelts from all Garou fallen in battle in order to try and &quot;promote&quot; devout Kin and fill out the ranks a little? I ask because if a Garou need not be killed specifically for the ritual than clearing out Hunter bases could yield the needed pelts to add to the tribes numbers and be a win win situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2135-disodium-benzoate","name":"DIsodium Benzoate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T08:11:21-08:00","id":60786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=60706#post60706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, because it's a tainted ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering Silver Record, according to the actual prop book, is written at least in part on BSD skin, it would be possible to purify the flesh. However, the ritual itself IS tainted if those garou who died did not give their flesh willingly, no matter which tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T10:56:05-08:00","id":60921,"title":"","content":"Disodium raises a good point there. Besides that, there isn't anything saying specifically that the skin dancers as a whole are opposed to the garou nation all together, just the vulture pack. Not only that, but with events within the skinner storyline one might argue that you could convince minotaur to be on the garou's side once more. Though from what I read, it seems he only truly hates black furies. Seems a lot of folk hate the furies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T11:28:41-08:00","id":60939,"title":"","content":"As we are discussing some other questions popped up, does it specifically say anywhere that the person benefiting from the rite be the one casting it? or could say, a single rite master perform the rite for others? if so, do both parties suffer from the taint or just the person performing the rite?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T09:19:26-08:00","id":61586,"title":"","content":"I don't think it works that way, but theres no reason you couldn't house rule it. Theres also the idea that 5 addled old garou could sacrifice themselves to be reborn to gaia's battle in a new body. Like passing down a fetish but its your flesh. Then you have a new chosen warrior of gaia, without the taint.<br /> <br /> Hell by that token, the garou could bolster some of their numbers a bit by just dragging their dead off the battlefield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T13:02:12-08:00","id":61689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=61586#post61586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it works that way, but theres no reason you couldn't house rule it. Theres also the idea that 5 addled old garou could sacrifice themselves to be reborn to gaia's battle in a new body. Like passing down a fetish but its your flesh. Then you have a new chosen warrior of gaia, without the taint.<br /> <br /> Hell by that token, the garou could bolster some of their numbers a bit by just dragging their dead off the battlefield.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the process to count as consenting, it has to involve a living individual giving up their life right then and there. Anything else would lack the impact and trickiness of the ceremony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T16:59:35-08:00","id":61836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=61689#post61689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For the process to count as consenting, it has to involve a living individual giving up their life right then and there. Anything else would lack the impact and trickiness of the ceremony.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like its time to create a new Rite of Organ Donor Consent to mark those who are willing donate themselves to the Rite of Sacred Rebirth lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T18:43:49-08:00","id":61910,"title":"","content":"Hell, I recall reading about a Get of Fenris fetish that was made by a Crinos form Garou voluntarily skinning himself to use his own pelt as the basis for an item (SpiritSkin p. 86 H&amp;K). If they can do that some really tough and/or masochistic Garou could make some serious steps twords promoting kinfolk to better warriors in this end of times. Hard earned pelts provided as reward to Kin that can make it through rigorous and brutal training for ready made Gaian warriors instead of hoping for new pups to live long enough to become useful.... I just got some ideas for a Metis camp that never seems to die out despite high death tolls and low recruitment from metis of other camps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2135-disodium-benzoate","name":"DIsodium Benzoate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T18:47:19-08:00","id":61911,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of story hooks here. This is some good stuff you guys! I myself am fond of the concept of the remorseful skin dancer pack looking to make good with gaia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-30T21:04:54-08:00","id":61977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=60939#post60939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As we are discussing some other questions popped up, does it specifically say anywhere that the person benefiting from the rite be the one casting it? or could say, a single rite master perform the rite for others? if so, do both parties suffer from the taint or just the person performing the rite?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rite as described on p. 213 of PGttG clearly states that the Ritemaster (i.e the person performing the Rite) is the one to whom the pelts are grafted. So, that would be yes, no and not relevant to your questions respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T05:23:29-08:00","id":62088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DIsodium Benzoate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=61910#post61910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, I recall reading about a Get of Fenris fetish that was made by a Crinos form Garou voluntarily skinning himself to use his own pelt as the basis for an item (SpiritSkin p. 86 H&amp;K). If they can do that some really tough and/or masochistic Garou could make some serious steps twords promoting kinfolk to better warriors in this end of times. Hard earned pelts provided as reward to Kin that can make it through rigorous and brutal training for ready made Gaian warriors instead of hoping for new pups to live long enough to become useful.... I just got some ideas for a Metis camp that never seems to die out despite high death tolls and low recruitment from metis of other camps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man..that fetish brought up a point I had never ever thought of... the rite calls for 5 pelts, with their healing factor who says one Garou can't donate his pelt more then once... Probably a good thing the Skin Dancers never took the alliance with the BSD. That is an extremely dark plot twist, pelt farms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:08:04-08:00","id":62119,"title":"","content":"I wonder if a Skin Dancer's pelt would be good enough to use as one of the five... Has that been mentioned anywhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T06:23:28-08:00","id":62127,"title":"","content":"I have read everything I could find on Samuel Haight and the Skin-Dancers since we started this conversation and it doesn't mention that, that I am aware of. Seems like the perfect Punishment Rite for a member of the Skin-Dancers... Skinned alive a number of times equal to the severity of your crime, extra pelts for the next rite of sacred rebirth... I think I am going to use that one in my next storyline lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T07:10:02-08:00","id":62143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=62088#post62088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh man..that fetish brought up a point I had never ever thought of... the rite calls for 5 pelts, with their healing factor who says one Garou can't donate his pelt more then once... Probably a good thing the Skin Dancers never took the alliance with the BSD. That is an extremely dark plot twist, pelt farms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Rite says they can't. This because it uses the adverb slain about the person who &quot;donates&quot; the pelt, thus indicating that healing factor or no, the subject who the pelt once belonged to must be deceased.<br /> <br /> So...no mass production of Skin-dancers...go figure, heh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T09:30:34-08:00","id":62237,"title":"","content":"That doesn't negate a mass production, as thats what the skinner sas sorta focuses on (among other things. Just means living garou can't make it happen. <br /> <br /> Course if this was new world there'd be some extra crazy ritual surrounding it that would bypass the restrictive nonsense. Spirits are prone to lying in that world. Though a skin dancer would probably be more akin to a skin thief from their respective book, and if they did go garou would probably be bale hounds. At any rate the social stigma for that would be IMO a lot worse in new world vs old. At best you'd be viewed as a bale hound. I doubt any of the First born would trust the individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T10:56:39-08:00","id":62309,"title":"","content":"Well, it negates mass production without accompanying mass murder, at least. Good enough for me.<br /> <br /> And I must admit I fail to see the relevance of all these references to Bale Hounds and other nWoD stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T11:41:18-08:00","id":62344,"title":"","content":"just thinking out loud is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:10:44-08:00","id":62358,"title":"","content":"Well if a certain Bear with the right motivations came along and started resurrecting Garou harvested for the rite... Maybe one or several with a serious grudge against the garou nation deciding that repeated death for the purpose of spawning a new gurhal and/or fera friendly werewolf tribe that actually is in balance with the others as the original plan went. Also doubling it as a punishment rite for those garou that seriously hinder fera instead of just any garou they find, We sentence you to 8 death sentences or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2135-disodium-benzoate","name":"DIsodium Benzoate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:24:26-08:00","id":62366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DIsodium Benzoate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=62358#post62358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if a certain Bear with the right motivations came along and started resurrecting Garou harvested for the rite... Maybe one or several with a serious grudge against the garou nation deciding that repeated death for the purpose of spawning a new gurhal and/or fera friendly werewolf tribe that actually is in balance with the others as the original plan went. Also doubling it as a punishment rite for those garou that seriously hinder fera instead of just any garou they find, We sentence you to 8 death sentences or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring the fact that 1) there aren't many Gurahl left, and 2) the Death Bear is quite likely to kill the one who challenges it. This is a solemn ceremony performed in desperate hope, not a reliable step in an assembly line. Also, you're still ignoring the taint of the Ritual of Secret Rebirth here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T12:35:31-08:00","id":62384,"title":"","content":"Yeah, any Elder Gurahl who's deranged enough to contemplate this is going to get killed very very soon by Mangi. So..it's largely a moot point. I doubt if anyone could fight the Death-Bear even enough time to make two pelts this way.<br /> <br /> And since I can't see any Garou being willing to go through something like that....we're at the point where the &quot;plan&quot; is apparently thus:<br /> <br /> I will repeatedly risk almost certain death in order to A) Torture another creature and B) Make a Wyrm tainted abomination. Hummmm....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T14:33:08-08:00","id":62469,"title":"","content":"I suppose you could have Garou who will their pelt to their sept on their death (Kind of like organ donors)? Does the prospective Skin Dancer have to kill the Garou themselves or just skin it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-31T14:45:21-08:00","id":62476,"title":"","content":"The Rite does say &quot;slain by the Ritemaster&quot; so yeah, that sort of rules out going around collecting pelts from fallen Garou. You actually have to kill them yourself. That said, it does seem to open for Garou giving themselves up willingly, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T00:50:29-08:00","id":62768,"title":"","content":"I might note though, that in skinner sas one of the Vulture pack has his mothers pelt incorporated into his fur, which was something that sam obtained, not him. Not disagreeing with the core books rules, but yeah. The skinner sas seems to have examples of not so direct rituals. Besides that the ritual is archaic. It could be that initially it requires the receiver to cast it upon himself, but there's nothing to say the rite didn't evolve through some manner of power spell sam found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T08:25:03-08:00","id":62914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=62768#post62768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might note though, that in skinner sas one of the Vulture pack has his mothers pelt incorporated into his fur, which was something that sam obtained, not him. Not disagreeing with the core books rules, but yeah. The skinner sas seems to have examples of not so direct rituals. Besides that the ritual is archaic. It could be that initially it requires the receiver to cast it upon himself, but there's nothing to say the rite didn't evolve through some manner of power spell sam found.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 does have some occasional consistency problems. Just read the writeup of the Okuma - it's one worthy of a TIME PARADOX! call out, since it mentions the werebears having a rivalry with the Kuei-jin before the Kuei-jin ever existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 02-01-2014, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T22:14:35-08:00","id":63295,"title":"","content":"I've always been of the opinion that there no taintless &quot;they gave me their skins willingly&quot; or &quot;i didn't kill anyone for the skins&quot; version of the Rite. At it's core, it is inherently evil and unwholesome. The sheer act of performing the ritual taints you to the core. Regardless of the source, you know 5 people had to be killed and SKINNED to perform the Rite.<br /> <br /> If you were to somehow cleanse yourself of this taint, it would burn away the Ritual as well, returning you to normal kinfolk status. However, the desire to keep your ill gotten and corrupted power would show you are not completely sorry about what you've done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2164-mistershifter","name":"MisterShifter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-01T22:50:08-08:00","id":63309,"title":"","content":"On the plus side you can get 7 points of merits!<br /> <br /> I think playing a skin dancer would be one of the more interesting characters one could play. Hell you'd already have a gnarly character back story. Then you get to deal with all the stigma of a Ronin, and then some.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-02-2014, 01:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T02:33:04-08:00","id":63356,"title":"","content":"I am very skeptical of the notion of not getting taint for it, too, but, to be fair, it is hinted at in the Rite. Then again, it is also described as &quot;blasphemous&quot; so, there's that...<br /> <br /> &quot;Stigma&quot; isn't quite the word I'd use. The Ronin are distrusted by Garou and spirits alike, yes. But they don't reek of the Wyrm and not usually killed on sight. Skin Dancers do and very likely will be if they try showing up at a random Sept.<br /> <br /> So....&quot;interesting&quot; perhaps in the &quot;unique snowflake&quot; way, but also not very playable in most stories, one would think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T05:02:21-07:00","id":94858,"title":"","content":"I have another question aside from the the main one that was asked before: could there be any non-Garou Kinfolk Skin Dancers too? I mean like Bastet, Gurahl, Ajaba, etc. Skin Dancers, or would the same Rite apply for such Kinfolk too? I've never ever read about such things, and I know one could always apply the Golden Rule, but what do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2554-sol","name":"Sol","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T06:10:19-07:00","id":94882,"title":"","content":"I suppose there could be such Skin Dancers. But given the often relatively solitary lifestyles of the other breeds and their therefore generally different realtionships with their kin, I'd say that it is very unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-20T06:27:03-07:00","id":94890,"title":"","content":"In the book that Haight is first introduced it mentions that he tried to hunt other more solitary breeds for their pelts but the ritual didn't work with those pelts. Now this doesn't mean that it wouldn't work for other breeds, it just sets a precedent that you have to have the pelts of the breed in which you are a kinfolk for because that is what you are spiritually attuned to. This is further supported by the rites used by the Corax and Camazotz, as members of the breed are created through their kinfolk and not spontaneously awakened like is common amongst other breeds. This fact that the Camazotz who are not avian in nature also use this kind of rite also gives some precedent to the fact that a none tainted version of the rite could be possible for the skin dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T09:17:06-07:00","id":117488,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for your answers!<br /> I knew that much that this would work only with the species one is spiritually attuned to, and about the Corax or Camazotz... and maybe my mind is limited, but I can't really imagine such things with the Rokea either... yeah okay the kin of an Inbetweener is always an option, but still. I wouldn't say this was unlikely, 'cause the Wyrms influence has just too many aspects, and it would really be a shame not to exploint the opportunities of such ideas when ones group is playing other breeds. If one always follows the preset rules, like creating a character according to the 13/9/5 rule, rather than creating one with 27 distributable points, one gets more stereotipical results. There could be kinfolk, who weren't that cared for by their shifter kin, and the Wyrm's influence can slip into even those places where other things can't go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2554-sol","name":"Sol","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T22:13:01-07:00","id":137714,"title":"","content":"So I'm reading the original &quot;when will you rage&quot; book, and there's a story with the Skinner himself in it. Now he's already a garou, but he's still collecting pelts and preparing them for the sacred rebirth. <br /> <br /> This implies that they don't need to hunt their own pelts necessarily. Unless the information in w20 is a retcon... but then the skinner sas came out after that.<br /> <br /> Another interesting thought: How does gameplay for the skinner sas change if the players are say... Skin dancers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T23:04:09-07:00","id":137787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=62914#post62914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 does have some occasional consistency problems. Just read the writeup of the Okuma - it's one worthy of a TIME PARADOX! call out, since it mentions the werebears having a rivalry with the Kuei-jin before the Kuei-jin ever existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> First off, we know pretty much nothing about the Wan Xian, except they were &quot;servants of heaven&quot; and they were immortals. Two other societies based on the &quot;Ten Thousand Immortals&quot; idea - the Hsien and Wu T'ian - <i>both</i> die nd return from the dead, as do the Wan Xian's descendant, the keui-Jin... so I don't think it's a huge assumption that the Wan Xian would have also worked off the idea of resurrection. Of couse, that probably made the werebears very uneasy. And the WoD being what it is, we have to assume the mortal-to-immortal process had flaws and throwbacks, and that individual immortals themselves became akuma, etc. e know that the fall of the Wan Xian took a while, and that by the time they instigated the War of Shame, the were fully in the hands of the Yama Kings.<br /> <br /> So imagine if you will, Wan Xian society is falling into demon worship. On the surface, they're still doing the &quot;Glorious service to the Heavens&quot; schtick, but otherwise, they're looking for the next Demon empror to give the guy a crown. The Okuma, ever paranoid about these dead-and-returning... <i>things</i> try to raise hte alarm. But well... they're dirty peasants, besmirching th good name of our friends, the divinely-chosen Wan Xian! You're always crying wolf, bear-face. Go eat some bamboo.<br /> <br /> Makes it pretty easy for the wallen Wan Xian to turn the courts on the bears, as a matter of honor. And of course. the Beast courts are hardly above corruption themselves, whether petty or spiritual...<br /> <br /> The book says they opposed the Kuei-Jin... because they did. The Wan Xian were damned well before instigating the War of Shame, and so they were probably on the Okuma's &quot;list&quot; - if they weren't qlready under careful scrutiny as Wan Xian in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T23:05:48-07:00","id":137789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=63309#post63309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the plus side you can get 7 points of merits!<br /> <br /> I think playing a skin dancer would be one of the more interesting characters one could play. Hell you'd already have a gnarly character back story. Then you get to deal with all the stigma of a Ronin, and then some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a gnarly backstory is <i>hardly</i> as fun as developing the character in a gnarly direction. That is, if you want to play a skin dancer, it's pobably more fun to play a Kinfolk seeking to join, than a ready-bade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T23:19:33-07:00","id":137796,"title":"","content":"Probably so. Like building up your reputation as a bale hound in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:27:07-07:00","id":138147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=137787#post137787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Not necessarily.<br /> <br /> First off, we know pretty much nothing about the Wan Xian, except they were &quot;servants of heaven&quot; and they were immortals. Two other societies based on the &quot;Ten Thousand Immortals&quot; idea - the Hsien and Wu T'ian - <i>both</i> die nd return from the dead, as do the Wan Xian's descendant, the keui-Jin... so I don't think it's a huge assumption that the Wan Xian would have also worked off the idea of resurrection. Of couse, that probably made the werebears very uneasy. And the WoD being what it is, we have to assume the mortal-to-immortal process had flaws and throwbacks, and that individual immortals themselves became akuma, etc. e know that the fall of the Wan Xian took a while, and that by the time they instigated the War of Shame, the were fully in the hands of the Yama Kings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wan Gui are supposed to be vastly different from their predecessors, who didn't go around acting like walking rape metaphors. At least...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So imagine if you will, Wan Xian society is falling into demon worship. On the surface, they're still doing the &quot;Glorious service to the Heavens&quot; schtick, but otherwise, they're looking for the next Demon empror to give the guy a crown. The Okuma, ever paranoid about these dead-and-returning... <i>things</i> try to raise hte alarm. But well... they're dirty peasants, besmirching th good name of our friends, the divinely-chosen Wan Xian! You're always crying wolf, bear-face. Go eat some bamboo. </div> </div> </div>Not where they could be found out. If they had done it so openly, everyone would have been crying for their destruction quite loudly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Makes it pretty easy for the wallen Wan Xian to turn the courts on the bears, as a matter of honor. And of course. the Beast courts are hardly above corruption themselves, whether petty or spiritual...<br /> <br /> The book says they opposed the Kuei-Jin... because they did. The Wan Xian were damned well before instigating the War of Shame, and so they were probably on the Okuma's &quot;list&quot; - if they weren't qlready under careful scrutiny as Wan Xian in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Having followed Exalted so closely for the past thirteen years, I am, at present, rather put out with &quot;Obi-Wan truths&quot;. Stop telling me it's true from a certain point of view and admit that you lied, made a continuity error, changed something deliberately, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T04:25:28-08:00","id":1191302,"title":"","content":"I've fought the Dead Bear and called back this thread into life.<br /> <br /> About SDs of other breeds: The W20 Shattered Dreams describes Jaguar Warriors of the Aztec Empire who uses the Rite of Sacred Rebirth to obtain their power.<br /> <br /> About the trip to Erebus: It clearly cleanse the Taint, and intention for absolution is not necessary. Check the Chaos Factor's 52 pg. You'll find a character, called Wanderer, who was/is a SD, but during her first trip to the Umbra angered some badass spirit who dipped her into the Silver Lake. She came out taint-free, but soon fallen into Harano.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T14:26:03-08:00","id":1191451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=1191302#post1191302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've fought the Dead Bear and called back this thread into life.<br /> <br /> About SDs of other breeds: The W20 Shattered Dreams describes Jaguar Warriors of the Aztec Empire who uses the Rite of Sacred Rebirth to obtain their power.<br /> <br /> About the trip to Erebus: It clearly cleanse the Taint, and intention for absolution is not necessary. Check the Chaos Factor's 52 pg. You'll find a character, called Wanderer, who was/is a SD, but during her first trip to the Umbra angered some badass spirit who dipped her into the Silver Lake. She came out taint-free, but soon fallen into Harano.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citing The Chaos Factor as an example of how anything in the WoD is supposed to work is like trying to establish a baseline of weapon power in BattleTech compared to modern-ish weapons and armor by using the half-serious April Fool's Joke supplement Experimental Technical Readout: 1945. Sure, it seems amusing, with KwK 43 shells harmlessly bouncing off of your ProtoMech armor when the gunners attempt to fire from far off, but it was never really intended to fulfill this function.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T23:01:27-08:00","id":1191850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/56544-skin-dancer-question?p=1191451#post1191451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Citing The Chaos Factor as an example of how anything in the WoD is supposed to work is like trying to establish a baseline of weapon power in BattleTech compared to modern-ish weapons and armor by using the half-serious April Fool's Joke supplement Experimental Technical Readout: 1945. Sure, it seems amusing, with KwK 43 shells harmlessly bouncing off of your ProtoMech armor when the gunners attempt to fire from far off, but it was never really intended to fulfill this function.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great simile, and I agree. But nothing contradicts (at my best knowledge) about that part from the newer materials. Dipping skinners in the Lakes should work. Probably would last for an eternity to clean some of them, but still effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}